Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", "choices": ["A) Furthermore,", "B) Meanwhile,", "C) However,", "D) Thus,"], "answer": "A", "explanation": "Choice A is the best answer. 'Furthermore' logically signals that the second sentence provides additional information about the intellectual accomplishments of the ancient Egyptians, building on their more well-known architectural achievements described in the first sentence.
Choice B is incorrect because 'meanwhile' illogically signals that the intellectual developments described occurred simultaneously but separately from their architectural achievements. Instead, both pieces of information describe aspects of ancient Egyptian sophistication. Choice C is incorrect because 'however' illogically signals a contrast or exception, which doesn't align with the logical continuation of accomplishments. Choice D is incorrect because 'thus' illogically signals a consequence or result."}

