What is the population of bacteria 9 hours after the start of the experiment?", "choices": ["A) 400", "B) 1600", "C) 1800", "D) 160"], "answer": "B", "explanation": "To evaluate $P(t)$ at $t = 9$, substitute $t = 9$ into the given function: $P(t) = 200 \cdot 2^{t/3}$. This becomes $P(9) = 200 \cdot 2^{9/3} = 200 \cdot 2^3 = 200 \cdot 8 = 1600$. Hence, the population of bacteria 9 hours after the start of the experiment is 1600, and the correct answer is B."}

