raw_json:
{"skill": "Unit Conversions", "difficulty": "Hard", "question": "A water tank has a capacity of 2,000 liters. How much is this capacity in gallons? (1 gallon = 3.785 liters)", "choices": ["A) 528.34", "B) 530.12", "C) 524.90", "D) 534.15"], "answer": "A", "explanation": "The given capacity of the tank is 2,000 liters. To convert this to gallons, use the relationship $1 \text{ gallon} = 3.785 \text{ liters}$. Divide the number of liters by 3.785:

\[ 2,000 \div 3.785 \approx 528.34 \]. 

Thus, the capacity in gallons is approximately \( 528.34 \), and the correct answer is \( \text{A} \). The other choices result from either multiplying instead of dividing or rounding errors."}

